      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_8",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Prince Robert Philippe Louis Eugène Ferdinand of Orléans, Duke of Chartres (November 9, 1840 – December 5, 1910) was the son of Prince Ferdinand Philippe, Duke of Orléans and thus grandson of King Louis-Philippe of France. He fought for the Union in the American Civil War, and then for France in the 1870 Franco-Prussian War. In 1863 he married his cousin Princess Françoise of Orléans in Kingston upon Thames – she was the daughter of François, Prince of Joinville. In 1886, he was exiled from France.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.1639920544807618,
      "temperature": 0.1639920544807618,
